Step 1: Open Cloudera Terminal
Open your Cloudera VM in VirtualBox, then select Applications → System Tools → Terminal.

Check whether Sqoop is installed:
sqoop version


Step 2: Start MySQL and create a database
Open the terminal and enter:
mysql -u root -p


Enter the password if prompted. At the MySQL prompt, run:
CREATE DATABASE labdb;
USE labdb;


Create a sample SQL table:
CREATE TABLE student (
    id INT,
    name VARCHAR(30),
    marks INT
);


Insert sample records:
INSERT INTO student VALUES
(1, 'Ravi', 85),
(2, 'Priya', 90),
(3, 'Arun', 78);


Verify:
SELECT * FROM student;


Exit MySQL:
exit;


Step 3: Create a Hive table
Open Hive:
hive


At the hive> prompt, create the destination table:
CREATE DATABASE IF NOT EXISTS labdb;
USE labdb;

CREATE TABLE student (
    id INT,
    name STRING,
    marks INT
)
ROW FORMAT DELIMITED
FIELDS TERMINATED BY ','
STORED AS TEXTFILE;


Exit Hive:
quit;


Step 4: Import SQL data into Hive using Sqoop
Run this command in the Linux terminal, not inside MySQL or Hive:
sqoop import \
--connect jdbc:mysql://localhost/labdb \
--username root \
--password cloudera \
--table student \
--hive-import \
--hive-table labdb.student \
--fields-terminated-by ',' \
--delete-target-dir \
-m 1

Step 5: Verify imported data in Hive
Open Hive:
hive


Run:
USE labdb;
SELECT * FROM student;


You should see the three student records.

Exit Hive:
quit;


Step 6: Export Hive data to the local machine
Sqoop exports database data, while hadoop fs -get downloads HDFS data to the local filesystem. To copy the Hive table's underlying HDFS files:
hadoop fs -ls /user/hive/warehouse/labdb.db/student


If that path exists, run:
hadoop fs -get /user/hive/warehouse/labdb.db/student ~/student_export


Check the local files:
ls ~/student_export


The exact HDFS location may differ depending on your Hive configuration.
Step 7: Export Hive data to SQL
First, ensure that the MySQL student table exists and contains no conflicting records. From the Linux terminal, run:
sqoop export \
--connect jdbc:mysql://localhost/labdb \
--username root \
--password cloudera \
--table student \
--export-dir /user/hive/warehouse/labdb.db/student \
--input-fields-terminated-by ',' \
-m 1


Purpose: Exports data stored in HDFS to the MySQL student table.

Purpose: Imports records from the MySQL student table into the Hive table labdb.student.
